    "title": "Man arrested in Guatemala for alleged rape, kidnapping of Orange County teen - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Knx News 97 1 Fm ,\n5 hours ago\nOrange County authorities tracked down a man they say kidnapped and raped a 13-year-old girl in Westminster.\nBrian Estuardo Verbena-Martinez was arrested in Guatemala and is awaiting extradition.\n“ [He’s] been charged with kidnapping a 13-year-old Orange County girl and repeatedly raping her over a period of hours,” Kimberly Edds with the OC DA’s office told KNX News’ Craig Fiegener.\nShe added that Martinez dropped the girl off at a friend’s house before fleeing to Guatemala.\n“This is actually the third capture of a wanted felon in a foreign country by the Orange County District Attorney's Office, as well as our federal partners and the FBI in the last about six weeks.\nIf convicted, Martinez faces a max sentence of life in prison without the possibility of parole.\nFollow KNX News 97.1 FM\nTwitter | Facebook | Instagram | TikTok",
